  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final standard sets an immediate 24-hour incident reporting duty that covers unconfirmed incidents, and a 72-hour customer notice. S2 keeps the 5% test figure only as a benchmark with no automatic sales bar, and it gives per-model numeric results to buyers and regulators without public per-model publication. S3 (12-month new-unit and 6-year retrofit deadlines) and S5 (mandatory 8-per-100k recall with no sales ban) are the most consequential for the two companies' flagship models."
